_______

This list is concerned primarily with discussion regarding
the use of ASUS brand motherboards, including I/O, SCSI, BIOS
setup, and other issues and concerns that may interest owners or
prospective owners.

These economical and fast OS/2, Linux, and DOS/Windows friendly boards 
include the 486 PCI based SP3 and newer "green" SP3G, as well as several 
Pentium models.  Given that the boards generally cost less than an 
Adaptec 2940 SCSI controller, they seems to be a great buy.

