Each month, Linux Journal includes a list of Linux consultants with
contact information.  We do this to help out the consultants, help out
new Linux users and to show "the world" that Linux is supported.

We encourage individuals and organizations who offer Linux support to
send us an entry for the directory.  Each entry consists of contact
information (name, address, phone, fax, e-mail) and a 1 or 2 sentence
description of what you do.  You can e-mail this information to
linux@ssc.com and put consultants directory in the subject line.  Space
permitting, you will be listed in the next issue of Linux Journal.
(Note that right now the next issue is October.  Besides our regular
distribution of 20,000 copies we will have a booth at Unix Expo and plan
to print an additional 5000 copies for that show.  A listing -- or an
advertisement if you are more than a consultant or want to say more -- in
this issue should pay off bigtime.)

Up until now the listings have been free.  But we now have to start
charging for a listing.  This is for two reasons: 1) people who pay
for a listing are more likely to be to serious and 2) we need to try
to recover some of our costs in producing the directory.

It is important that we continue to show that Linux support is available
so we have the following new policy:
  * Your initial (1-time) listing in the directory is free
  * A 12-month listing is $150 and you can charge it on a credit
    card

I feel this offers an amazing value.  If you have any questions or want to
