sold does NOT equal and cannot be anywhere near the number of people using 
Linux, but it is certainly a measure of how much money the Linux community
has.
 
These figures are simply raw data, and all raw data can be turned into lies, 
damn lies and statistics. I have not tried to interpret these figures in 
any way, as that would be utterly meaningless, depending on factors such 
as price of cd's, the fact that some Linux disk are in fact sets of 2 disks, 
